{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1512301-playing-as-the-enemies","id":1512301,"title":"Playing as the enemies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-21T14:21:50-07:00","id":1512301,"title":"Playing as the enemies","content":"Someone already plays facing the Garou Nation, and I don't mean being a BSD, or a Formori, I mean as a human member of Pentex, a head of security for example and having to defend against the Garou or even plan attacks against them. If so, how was the experience?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T14:31:18-07:00","id":1512304,"title":"","content":"I can't say I've played a normal human employee of Pentex before, but having played a human journalist investigating things that were caused by local Garou... it's extremely unfulfilling. Humans without powers, even with really high stats like Willpower, basically can't ever do anything interesting. You either get killed, or you get discredited and neutralized that way.<br /> <br /> The head of security at a Pentex owned facility is basically going to either be unable to do anything about the Garou targeting them, or resort to calling in back up from someone that can and hide in hopes of surviving.<br /> <br /> The WoD is very purposefully stacked against humans without powers. The only advantage humans really have is a huge numerical advantage, and any supernatural foe with a damn is going to try to kill off the leaders and organizers of a massive mob targeting their kind (aka the PCs in this sort of setup), because trying to cause the mob to lose internal coherence is the only way to really stop it rather than get out of its way and hope the damage when it subsides isn't too bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T20:36:59-07:00","id":1512536,"title":"","content":"We played a one-shot First Team game.....we were eaten by the Fomorach we were trying to corral before we even engaged Garou. Was a bit of gory fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T11:01:47-07:00","id":1512750,"title":"","content":"I haven\u2019t personally, aside from the occasional troupe play scenario.<br /> <br /> That said I do think there is an interesting meta-quality that comes from playing antagonist splats, like Black Spiral Dancers or what have you. In a sense the whole concept of the World of Darkness is to play the monster antagonists of traditional horror works but I think that in some cases the reverse of circumstances leads the monsters to begin more like protagonists then we may have originally envisioned. I can certainly see something like playing BSD be a movement in the opposite direction for those who were impacted by the appeals of the premise of playing a traditional antagonist role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}